From 79e9d853b0fb083a363cf1278d40b915e892d51b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Kearney <303316+iconidentify@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 20:35:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8103: describe tunneled PCIe state
 restore
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Kensington USB devices can disappear after s2idle even when the initial
port restart and cable health check succeed. A later PCIe link failure
must trigger another fresh validation instead of waiting for a cable
interrupt or manual replug.

Restore the resettable M1 tunneled host and DART state before restarting
the downstream link. Gate DART commands and fault handling around clock
shutdown, preserve stream selection, and describe the reset and register
initialization properties in the binding.

Gate Type-C work across initialization, sleep and removal, read fresh
cable metadata after resume, and preserve an unchanged healthy session.
Propagate late link failures through an atomic switch notification into
bounded process-context revalidation. Keep failure history sticky while
allowing later notifications from a retained host. Failed reads or health
checks request a bounded reconnect; successful checks preserve routing.
Keep failed display-route acquisition retryable.

Add state-machine and DART regression coverage. The native ARM64 build
and 88 KUnit cases pass. Two M1/j293 Kensington USB-only suspend cycles
exercised late link-loss recovery and restored usable input without a
manual replug. The initiating xHCI resume fault remains unresolved.

[ryan: adapted to 7.2.10 — split: DT part only; driver and binding parts go with 170-usb]
Signed-off-by: Chris Kearney <303316+iconidentify@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8103.dtsi | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8103.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8103.dtsi
index ba13c756900c55..ea073c207c014b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8103.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8103.dtsi
@@ -1681,6 +1681,7 @@
 				interrupt-parent = <&aic>;
 				interrupts = <AIC_IRQ 770 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 				power-domains = <&ps_atc0_pcie>;
+				resets = <&ps_atc0_pcie>;
 
 				msi-controller;
 				msi-parent = <&apciec0>;
@@ -1906,6 +1907,7 @@
 				interrupt-parent = <&aic>;
 				interrupts = <AIC_IRQ 850 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 				power-domains = <&ps_atc1_pcie>;
+				resets = <&ps_atc1_pcie>;
 
 				msi-controller;
 				msi-parent = <&apciec1>;
